---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Contribute" description="How to add a project, paper or dataset to the Slay the Spire Dev index.">
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Add to the index</h1>
    <p>Each entry is one Markdown file. Open a pull request with a new file, or open an issue if you'd rather someone else write it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap prose body">
    <h2>Add a project</h2>
    <p>Create <code>src/content/projects/your-project.md</code>:</p>
    <pre><code>{`---
name: Your Project
url: https://github.com/you/your-project
repo: you/your-project
author: you
games: [sts1]
category: bot
approaches: [search]
language: Python
license: MIT
status: active
summary: One or two plain sentences on what it does, under 240 characters.
---

Optional longer notes: how it works, what it depends on, and any results
with the settings they were measured under.`}</code></pre>
    <ul>
      <li><code>games</code>: <code>sts1</code>, <code>sts2</code>, or both.</li>
      <li><code>category</code>: <code>interface</code>, <code>modding</code>, <code>library</code>, <code>bot</code>, <code>simulator</code>, <code>dataset</code>, <code>tool</code> or <code>research</code>.</li>
      <li><code>approaches</code>: any of <code>rules</code>, <code>search</code>, <code>rl</code>, <code>imitation</code>, <code>llm</code>, <code>tooling</code>.</li>
      <li><code>status</code>: <code>active</code>, <code>maintained</code>, <code>dormant</code> or <code>archived</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What makes a good entry</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Describe what the project does in plain words, the way its own README would.</li>
      <li>Only quote numbers the project publishes, with character, ascension, game version and run count.</li>
      <li>Status follows the last commit: active within six months, maintained within eighteen, dormant after that.</li>
      <li>Papers and datasets live in <code>src/content/papers/</code> and <code>src/content/datasets/</code> with similar fields.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Run it locally</h2>
    <pre><code>npm install
npm run dev</code></pre>
    <p>The build checks every entry against the schema, so a missing or misspelled field fails before it reaches the site.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/ptrlrd/slaythespire-dev">Open the repository</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .body {
    padding: 8px 0 80px;
  }
</style>
